### Session 12 Lab: the secured Library API (IntelliJ HTTP client or VS Code REST Client)
### Every seeded account has the password secret123:
###   sara@example.com (MEMBER, id 1), omar@example.com (MEMBER, id 2), librarian@example.com (LIBRARIAN, id 3)
@base = http://localhost:8080/api

### 1. No token -> 401 with "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer"
GET {{base}}/books

### 2. Wrong password -> 401, same message as an unknown email
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "wrong-password" }

### 3. Log in as Sara and keep the token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "sara@example.com", "password": "secret123" }

> {% client.global.set("sara", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 4. Log in as the librarian and keep the token
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "librarian@example.com", "password": "secret123" }

> {% client.global.set("librarian", response.body.accessToken); %}

### 5. Who am I?
GET {{base}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 6. Any member may read the catalogue -> 200
GET {{base}}/books?author=orwell
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 7. ... but not change it -> 403
POST {{base}}/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sara's favourite author" }

### 8. The librarian may -> 201
POST {{base}}/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Radwa Ashour" }

### 9. Sara borrows for herself (no memberId needed) -> 201
POST {{base}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 1 }

### 10. Sara tries to borrow for Omar -> 403
POST {{base}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 3, "memberId": 2 }

### 11. The librarian borrows for Omar at the desk -> 201
POST {{base}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 3, "memberId": 2 }

### 12. The librarian forgets memberId -> 400
POST {{base}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "bookId": 5 }

### 13. Sara's own loans -> 200
GET {{base}}/members/1/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 14. Omar's loans, asked by Sara -> 404 (not 403: a stranger must not learn what exists)
GET {{base}}/members/2/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 15. Sara returns Omar's loan -> 404. Use the id from request 11.
PATCH {{base}}/loans/3/return
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 16. Only the librarian may list all members -> 403 for Sara
GET {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{sara}}

### 17. The librarian creates a member with a first password -> 201 (no password in the answer)
POST {{base}}/members
Authorization: Bearer {{librarian}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Nour Adel", "email": "nour@example.com", "password": "welcome123" }

### 18. The new member logs in -> 200
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nour@example.com", "password": "welcome123" }

### 19. A broken token -> 401
GET {{base}}/books
Authorization: Bearer not-a-real-token
